'''Eye of Malice''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Callous Mask}}.

== Mechanics ==
{{status
| name                   = Eye of Malice
| type                   = Debuff
| description = {{c|normal|You have increased Fire and Cold Resistances}}
| bonuses = 50% increased Fire and Cold Resistances
}}

At first glance the mod {{c|mod|Nearby Enemies have 50% increased Fire and Cold Resistances}} may sound unhelpful; however, it also multiplies negative [[resistance]]s.<ref>[[:File:Eye_of_Mallice_Resistance_Test_in_PvP.png|Data gathered by user:13tayler13 in PVP.]]</ref>

For example, if a monster's Cold Resistance was lowered to -30% via sources such as [[Exposure]], [[Frostbite]], [[Void Beacon]], and other methods, Eye of Malice's effect would cause that monster to have -45% instead. Note that this modifier affects the actual resistance (or tooltip resistance) of the monster; it '''does not scale on player side''' by how many -#% to monster resistances with any given method (i.e. the scaling is calculated on monster side). Conversely, a monster with 30% Cold Resistance after applying any player's aura/curse/other #% res effect, will have 45% Cold Resistance instead. Therefore, it is important to stack lots of sources of Resistance stripping to get the monster negative.

Note that Penetration applies after this step; the Penetration value itself will not increase. Read [[Receiving damage]] and [[Resistance penetration]] for details.

Alternatively, you can use this item with effects that invert enemy resistances like {{il|Rakiata's Dance}} and {{il|Wild Strike of Extremes}}, though it has some slight anti-synergy with its exposure effect. For this, you need to avoid getting effects that give reduced resistances or increased exposure effect.

The [[Nearby]] radius is 3 metre.
